It looks like you're encountering a "Redeclaration Error" because the constant CurrencyMasterStyles is being defined and exported in the same file where you are using the main component (CurrencyMaster.js).
In JavaScript/React, you can only declare a variable or constant once within a single scope.
The file structure I provided previously assumed that CurrencyMasterStyles was either imported from a separate file (e.g., ./CurrencyMasterStyles.js) or that you were putting the styles at the very end of the main component file. When the bundler processes the file, it sees two separate declarations/uses for CurrencyMasterStyles.
🛠️ Solution: Move Styles to a Separate File
To fix this, you must separate the style object into its own file and then import it into CurrencyMaster.js.
Here are the two updated files:
1. Create a New File: CurrencyMasterStyles.js
Move the style object definition entirely into a new file named CurrencyMasterStyles.js (or similar, based on your project structure).
